1
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:32,990
Damn it! You're kidding me!

2
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:35,510
This wall wasn't here last time! What gives?

3
00:01:36,790 --> 00:01:37,870
Another earthquake?

4
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:40,030
That's not what that was.

5
00:01:40,290 --> 00:01:42,770
The dungeon is moving and changing its shape.

6
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:45,250
I bet that mage is doing it.

7
00:01:45,830 --> 00:01:48,050
He's probably being cautious about us.

8
00:01:48,670 --> 00:01:52,330
Does that mean we'll be wandering around this place in circles till we die?

9
00:01:53,170 --> 00:01:55,170
Guess I've got to get a bit reckless.

10
00:01:55,930 --> 00:01:56,810
Just wait here!

11
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:06,590
The coast is clear.

12
00:02:08,390 --> 00:02:11,270
Looks like climbing the wall might not be such a great idea.

13
00:02:12,190 --> 00:02:14,030
Well, it's time to start walking then.

14
00:02:16,150 --> 00:02:19,870
I don't know if anyone else is getting this feeling, but...

15
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:22,570
It's like the town is getting livelier.

16
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:26,810
With the Red Dragon dead, the monsters hiding from it are surfacing.

17
00:02:27,170 --> 00:02:29,690
This floor originally had lots of monsters.

18
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:32,350
Us avoiding them with sheer good love.

19
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:37,330
Whoa, are you guys all right?

20
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:39,910
Hmm, so unhealthy.

21
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:44,370
We've been walking non-stop and haven't had a decent meal since eating the dragon.

22
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:47,930
If I had to guess Laios' age...

23
00:02:47,930 --> 00:02:50,590
Well, I can't really tell if he's young or old simply by looking.

24
00:02:51,010 --> 00:02:54,370
But Chilchuk and Marcel are definitely still growing.

25
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:55,350
Come on.

26
00:02:55,350 --> 00:03:00,650
I'm overwhelmed with shame that I can't provide a hearty meal at such an important time in their lives.

27
00:03:00,990 --> 00:03:02,190
I must feed them.

28
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:03,950
The young'uns must be fed.

29
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:05,850
And I have to feed them!

30
00:03:06,850 --> 00:03:09,030
Hmm, I smell something kind of sweet.

31
00:03:09,450 --> 00:03:10,370
Something you can eat?

32
00:03:10,370 --> 00:03:13,670
No, it's more like a floral scent.

33
00:03:14,410 --> 00:03:17,210
Wherever flowers are blooming, there's sure to be some water.

34
00:03:17,730 --> 00:03:19,410
It's all up to you, Chilchuk.

35
00:03:19,510 --> 00:03:20,190
I'm on it!

36
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:27,290
Is this place some kind of graveyard?

37
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:32,330
Wait, what's that over there?

38
00:03:38,330 --> 00:03:39,290
Don't look!

39
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:43,910
Oh, excuse us.

40
00:03:44,170 --> 00:03:45,670
Hey, Senshi, let go!

41
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:49,510
Get back, Senshi!

42
00:03:54,810 --> 00:03:55,690
What's that?

43
00:03:56,250 --> 00:03:57,070
Arm yourselves!

44
00:03:57,690 --> 00:03:59,150
These things aren't humans.

45
00:03:59,730 --> 00:04:01,670
They're dry-head flowers.

46
00:04:01,930 --> 00:04:03,750
Then there's dust in the air is.

47
00:04:04,310 --> 00:04:05,910
It's not dust at all.

48
00:04:05,910 --> 00:04:11,210
Once inhaled, these microparticles cling to the respiratory system's mucous membrane.

49
00:04:12,010 --> 00:04:15,390
The body recognizes these particles and labels them as harmful.

50
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:20,210
Then activates its immune system and quickly tries to dispel them.

51
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:21,990
Simply put,

52
00:04:23,490 --> 00:04:26,270
it's hay fever.

53
00:04:26,630 --> 00:04:26,950
Ew!

54
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:28,510
This is so gross!

55
00:04:30,690 --> 00:04:32,010
Try its pollen!

56
00:04:32,210 --> 00:04:32,710
No way!

57
00:04:33,410 --> 00:04:33,850
Crap!

58
00:04:34,310 --> 00:04:35,170
Don't inhale it!

59
00:04:39,810 --> 00:04:41,130
This is bad!

60
00:04:41,190 --> 00:04:42,730
I can't stop crying!

61
00:04:42,730 --> 00:04:42,890
I can't stop crying!

62
00:04:45,670 --> 00:04:48,750
Come on, Senshi!

63
00:04:49,010 --> 00:04:50,090
You gotta stand up!

64
00:04:51,070 --> 00:04:51,590
Loyal!

65
00:04:51,730 --> 00:04:53,050
I can't escape!

66
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:54,250
Where are you?

67
00:04:55,150 --> 00:04:56,330
My eyes!

68
00:04:58,490 --> 00:05:00,090
Senshi, reach forward!

69
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:01,210
On my signal,

70
00:05:01,550 --> 00:05:03,590
I want you to swing that sword behind you!

71
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:04,670
Ready?

72
00:05:05,730 --> 00:05:06,670
And...

73
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:07,950
Swing!

74
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:17,610
My eyes are suddenly getting itchy!

75
00:05:18,210 --> 00:05:19,870
My vision is...

76
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:28,610
Run, Senshi!

77
00:05:28,850 --> 00:05:29,210
No!

78
00:05:29,550 --> 00:05:32,730
It's my job to stay here and protect all the young'uns from harm!

79
00:05:32,730 --> 00:05:34,290
What are you talking about?

80
00:05:34,470 --> 00:05:34,990
Jilchuk!

81
00:05:35,230 --> 00:05:36,950
I'm gonna need you to be my eyes!

82
00:05:37,190 --> 00:05:37,670
Tau!

83
00:05:37,730 --> 00:05:38,830
I can't see anything!

84
00:05:39,470 --> 00:05:42,010
Your five senses are better than most, aren't they?

85
00:05:43,570 --> 00:05:44,050
Smell.

86
00:05:44,790 --> 00:05:45,170
No.

87
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:47,410
The scent of the pollen is too strong.

88
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:49,230
Sound.

89
00:05:49,230 --> 00:05:52,890
Senshi's sneezing is too loud!

90
00:05:53,170 --> 00:05:55,830
I can't trust my sight, smell, or hearing right now.

91
00:05:56,350 --> 00:05:57,050
I know!

92
00:05:57,730 --> 00:05:58,590
It's the wind!

93
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:03,050
It thought you'd sneeze and move to your back right!

94
00:06:03,470 --> 00:06:05,390
Swing up in that direction, Senshi!

95
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:15,430
Ken-skei...

96
00:06:15,430 --> 00:06:19,030
It completely snapped in two.

97
00:06:19,470 --> 00:06:22,610
I need to repair it and feed it some mana quickly or it'll die.

98
00:06:23,230 --> 00:06:26,970
And after it took me so many years to get it to grow this much...

99
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:28,090
Hmm?

100
00:06:30,590 --> 00:06:31,110
This...

101
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:32,870
This whole area is safe!

102
00:06:32,910 --> 00:06:33,850
You're such a liar!

103
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:36,790
You guys fought against dryad flowers?

104
00:06:37,670 --> 00:06:39,230
That must have been rough.

105
00:06:39,230 --> 00:06:41,230
So they were flower monsters, huh?

106
00:06:41,950 --> 00:06:44,530
And here I was thinking they were human men and women.

107
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:47,250
The male and female part was right.

108
00:06:47,430 --> 00:06:48,690
Dryads are unisexual.

109
00:06:49,270 --> 00:06:49,430
Oh!

110
00:06:49,730 --> 00:06:50,570
Hang on a minute!

111
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:52,630
He's doing it again.

112
00:06:53,030 --> 00:06:55,050
Think we should knock him out to stop him this time?

113
00:06:55,490 --> 00:06:58,790
I feel like we've gotten to a point where we can't be picky anymore.

114
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:01,130
I found myself having thoughts like,

115
00:07:01,250 --> 00:07:03,370
so what if the flower is shaped like a human?

116
00:07:04,210 --> 00:07:04,650
Marcy.

117
00:07:04,650 --> 00:07:04,930
Ah!

118
00:07:04,930 --> 00:07:05,030
Ah!

119
00:07:05,030 --> 00:07:05,430
Ah!

120
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:05,530
Ah!

121
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:05,650
Ah!

122
00:07:05,650 --> 00:07:05,670
Ah!

123
00:07:05,670 --> 00:07:05,750
Ah!

124
00:07:06,750 --> 00:07:07,930
Found some!

125
00:07:08,930 --> 00:07:10,890
Beautiful dryad fruit!

126
00:07:11,890 --> 00:07:14,110
How do I reverse time?

127
00:07:14,110 --> 00:07:14,690
Cut it out!

128
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:16,890
Don't casually look for scary-sounding spells!

129
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:18,730
Your black magic jokes aren't funny,

130
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:20,030
so seriously stop!

131
00:07:21,090 --> 00:07:24,590
I didn't see a lick of pollen come out of this last dryad I cut down.

132
00:07:25,630 --> 00:07:26,930
The female flower, then.

133
00:07:27,690 --> 00:07:28,770
Before pollination,

134
00:07:29,130 --> 00:07:31,170
flowers care for and protect the other fruit.

135
00:07:32,850 --> 00:07:35,150
Hey, this thing kinda looks like fruit, too.

136
00:07:35,490 --> 00:07:36,150
Yeah, good find.

137
00:07:36,450 --> 00:07:37,550
Those are flower buds.

138
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:39,850
They're what eventually becomes the dryad flower.

139
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:43,950
They look tasty and much easier to eat than the stuff you're carrying.

140
00:07:44,310 --> 00:07:45,590
What's the worst that could happen?

141
00:07:46,110 --> 00:07:46,990
Let's grab a few.

142
00:07:49,890 --> 00:07:51,330
Don't pluck too many of them.

143
00:07:51,490 --> 00:07:51,870
Got it?

144
00:07:54,630 --> 00:07:55,030
Understood.

145
00:07:56,170 --> 00:07:56,570
Whoa!

146
00:07:56,930 --> 00:07:58,270
There are mandrakes growing here.

147
00:07:58,570 --> 00:07:59,650
There's no dog around,

148
00:07:59,730 --> 00:08:01,750
so we'll just have to chop off their heads, okay?

149
00:08:01,910 --> 00:08:02,230
Hmm.

150
00:08:02,770 --> 00:08:03,790
Seriously, Chill Chuck?

151
00:08:03,790 --> 00:08:05,210
Can you drop that already?

152
00:08:06,710 --> 00:08:07,110
Hmm.

153
00:08:07,710 --> 00:08:10,250
A pretty good harvest, if I say so myself.

154
00:08:10,570 --> 00:08:11,730
I'm glad I thought ahead

155
00:08:11,730 --> 00:08:13,850
and asked to borrow this axe from those orcs.

156
00:08:14,010 --> 00:08:14,410
Chee!

157
00:08:15,230 --> 00:08:17,910
Put the chopped ingredients into a pot with water

158
00:08:17,910 --> 00:08:19,070
and bring to a boil.

159
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:20,950
When they become soft,

160
00:08:21,130 --> 00:08:22,150
remove them from the heat

161
00:08:22,150 --> 00:08:24,290
and give them a good mashing in the pot.

162
00:08:25,290 --> 00:08:26,830
Once it becomes paste-like,

163
00:08:27,050 --> 00:08:30,030
add some more water along with your preferred seasonings.

164
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:31,250
Hmm.

165
00:08:31,250 --> 00:08:31,450
Hmm.

166
00:08:33,790 --> 00:08:37,690
It already smells good.

167
00:08:38,150 --> 00:08:39,310
In that case,

168
00:08:39,890 --> 00:08:41,510
lightly fry it in some butter

169
00:08:41,510 --> 00:08:43,090
and then add in some mushrooms.

170
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:46,330
Pour a little melted cheese over the top

171
00:08:46,330 --> 00:08:48,570
and it's ready.

172
00:08:51,610 --> 00:08:53,350
Why'd you put it in that thing?

173
00:08:53,710 --> 00:08:55,230
I figured it might give you some help

174
00:08:55,230 --> 00:08:56,430
with replenishing your mana.

175
00:08:56,850 --> 00:08:58,170
You can have good intentions,

176
00:08:58,370 --> 00:09:00,030
but that doesn't make doing it any better.

177
00:09:00,530 --> 00:09:01,730
I'll still eat it, though.

178
00:09:01,730 --> 00:09:04,270
It's sweet!

179
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:06,010
There's a floral fragrance,

180
00:09:06,150 --> 00:09:07,450
and despite it being dense,

181
00:09:07,510 --> 00:09:08,730
it melts in your mouth.

182
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:10,230
I love this.

183
00:09:11,450 --> 00:09:12,850
That's kind of horrifying.

184
00:09:12,850 --> 00:09:20,090
The acidity of the cheese works well.

185
00:09:20,310 --> 00:09:22,450
I personally like how there's a slight bitterness.

186
00:09:24,150 --> 00:09:25,070
So now what?

187
00:09:25,310 --> 00:09:27,010
How do we escape from this place?

188
00:09:27,350 --> 00:09:29,110
What if we end up stuck in here forever?

189
00:09:30,110 --> 00:09:31,550
Sealing the path to the surface

190
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:32,830
will cut the flow of magic,

191
00:09:32,830 --> 00:09:35,870
so I highly doubt he'd try to keep us here indefinitely.

192
00:09:36,570 --> 00:09:38,450
Which means there has to be a way out.

193
00:09:38,450 --> 00:09:41,710
Do you think there's any kind of logic

194
00:09:41,710 --> 00:09:42,790
to the dungeon changes?

195
00:09:43,410 --> 00:09:44,170
That's it!

196
00:09:44,290 --> 00:09:46,550
I'll record the frequency of the earthquakes on the map.

197
00:09:46,690 --> 00:09:48,630
I'm starting to think this might work out.

198
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:50,610
It's a lot easier to feel optimistic

199
00:09:50,610 --> 00:09:52,110
when your stomach's full, huh?

200
00:09:52,110 --> 00:09:58,570
My body's all nice and toasty now.

201
00:09:58,830 --> 00:10:00,910
Seems like some of my mana is back, too.

202
00:10:01,530 --> 00:10:04,090
Laios, Senshi, we should get your wounds healed up.

203
00:10:04,310 --> 00:10:06,330
You don't need to push yourself this soon.

204
00:10:06,510 --> 00:10:07,350
I'm not healing.

205
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:08,890
You are.

206
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:10,590
You really need to step up.

207
00:10:11,850 --> 00:10:13,870
It's time for me to teach you magic.

208
00:10:14,590 --> 00:10:16,330
I won't be able to protect everybody

209
00:10:16,330 --> 00:10:18,110
from the Mad Mage all by myself.

210
00:10:18,110 --> 00:10:21,210
If you can learn healing and abjuration magic,

211
00:10:21,410 --> 00:10:22,850
it'll make things easier.

212
00:10:23,610 --> 00:10:25,430
Fallon taught you the basics, didn't she?

213
00:10:25,690 --> 00:10:26,730
More or less.

214
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:29,610
She actually specialized in the Gnome magic system,

215
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:31,650
which is a bit different from the magic system

216
00:10:31,650 --> 00:10:32,790
I learned to use.

217
00:10:33,010 --> 00:10:35,690
But the roots are similar, so it should be okay.

218
00:10:35,990 --> 00:10:37,990
I'll drum it into your head fast, I swear.

219
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:41,550
Let's do this.

220
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:42,650
And get stronger.

221
00:10:42,650 --> 00:10:48,390
They're too optimistic about this.

222
00:10:48,870 --> 00:10:51,730
And that's exactly how young people should be.

223
00:10:53,230 --> 00:10:55,890
Can you stop treating me like a child already, Senshi?

224
00:10:56,110 --> 00:10:57,610
I'm so tired of it!

225
00:10:57,810 --> 00:11:00,490
Why'd you even cover my eyes in front of those dryads anyway?

226
00:11:00,890 --> 00:11:02,610
I mean, you saved me, but still!

227
00:11:03,610 --> 00:11:04,410
I see.

228
00:11:05,190 --> 00:11:06,070
Well, Chilchuk,

229
00:11:06,490 --> 00:11:09,210
you said before that your old man passed away, didn't you?

230
00:11:10,110 --> 00:11:11,530
Yeah, what about it?

231
00:11:11,530 --> 00:11:12,050
Hmm.

232
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:14,630
Now is as good a time as any.

233
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:16,810
I'll teach you what you need to know.

234
00:11:17,770 --> 00:11:19,190
Go and take a seat right there.

235
00:11:20,490 --> 00:11:22,070
You're probably at the age

236
00:11:22,070 --> 00:11:24,770
where you're gonna start showing interest in certain things,

237
00:11:25,090 --> 00:11:27,390
so you're gonna need to have some good knowledge about them.

238
00:11:27,910 --> 00:11:28,830
What's that mean?

239
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:32,190
Let's just say that humans also have a stamen and pistol.

240
00:11:34,350 --> 00:11:35,870
Wrong! Do it again!

241
00:11:36,230 --> 00:11:37,250
Are you listening?

242
00:11:37,250 --> 00:11:42,710
And so their lessons continued on well into the night.

243
00:11:44,790 --> 00:11:46,250
Come on, do it.

244
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:53,430
The hell?

245
00:11:53,430 --> 00:11:57,370
I thought touching it softly might be kind of weird.

246
00:11:57,510 --> 00:11:59,530
That's not the point at all, so get over it!

247
00:11:59,890 --> 00:12:00,970
Give me your left hand.

248
00:12:03,530 --> 00:12:04,010
See?

249
00:12:04,430 --> 00:12:05,950
Something like this is fine.

250
00:12:07,230 --> 00:12:10,510
Your magic won't improve if things like this embarrass you.

251
00:12:10,670 --> 00:12:11,630
Come on, focus!

252
00:12:11,630 --> 00:12:15,850
You need to become aware of the mana that flows within your body.

253
00:12:16,290 --> 00:12:17,710
It's like the Venus system.

254
00:12:18,370 --> 00:12:20,530
Link that flow with the palm of your hand,

255
00:12:20,950 --> 00:12:24,630
from the very top of your head and all the way down to my toes.

256
00:12:25,250 --> 00:12:26,350
Match to my breathing,

257
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:28,530
my body temp and pulse.

258
00:12:29,050 --> 00:12:31,050
When you feel like you have the rhythm down,

259
00:12:31,330 --> 00:12:32,270
repeat after me.

260
00:12:32,270 --> 00:12:46,010
It itches!

261
00:12:47,610 --> 00:12:48,810
It's so itchy!

262
00:12:49,510 --> 00:12:50,630
Are you all right?

263
00:12:50,950 --> 00:12:51,430
What the?

264
00:12:51,810 --> 00:12:53,330
The scap just came off.

265
00:12:53,710 --> 00:12:55,850
Wow, you actually did it!

266
00:12:55,950 --> 00:12:57,030
Good job, Lyos!

267
00:12:57,230 --> 00:12:58,510
Are you sure about that?

268
00:12:58,710 --> 00:12:59,990
Your ear is bleeding now.

269
00:13:00,330 --> 00:13:02,330
It's fine, that's how it is at the start.

270
00:13:02,630 --> 00:13:04,050
You're a pretty fast learner.

271
00:13:04,630 --> 00:13:06,930
I guess your bloodline has a talent for it.

272
00:13:07,570 --> 00:13:10,450
It helps that the way you teach was easy for me to follow.

273
00:13:11,230 --> 00:13:12,050
Go ahead to here.

274
00:13:13,010 --> 00:13:15,810
Now, before you forget what that feeling is like,

275
00:13:16,210 --> 00:13:17,130
try it on Senshi.

276
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:21,870
I'll be watching, so just go and do it like before.

277
00:13:23,150 --> 00:13:24,190
It's makeshift,

278
00:13:24,190 --> 00:13:27,390
but I'm going to use some dryad branches to repair it.

279
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:29,150
Hopefully it works.

280
00:13:29,990 --> 00:13:34,730
Did it have to be there?

281
00:13:34,910 --> 00:13:35,590
Oh, I...

282
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:37,490
You need to quit worrying about that!

283
00:13:37,810 --> 00:13:39,710
You can't stay shy about it!

284
00:13:40,190 --> 00:13:41,950
Embarrassment's improvement's biggest enemy.

285
00:13:42,950 --> 00:13:45,430
You shouldn't really disregard that sort of stuff.

286
00:13:46,290 --> 00:13:48,230
Healers touch other people more than anyone,

287
00:13:48,350 --> 00:13:49,690
and it can lead to some problems.

288
00:13:50,510 --> 00:13:53,570
Personal relationships are the main reason parties disband.

289
00:13:53,570 --> 00:13:57,950
Jealousy, envy, falling in and out of love, grudges and hate.

290
00:13:58,590 --> 00:14:00,010
It's a real nuisance.

291
00:14:00,370 --> 00:14:03,450
You wouldn't happen to be talking about Fallon and Shuro.

292
00:14:03,610 --> 00:14:05,270
I'm speaking from experience.

293
00:14:05,730 --> 00:14:07,730
For leaders, instead of combat skills,

294
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:10,030
they should focus on keeping their team together.

295
00:14:10,030 --> 00:14:12,710
Honestly, instead of him learning magic,

296
00:14:12,990 --> 00:14:15,990
I'd rather he develop good social skills and judge of character.

297
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:18,230
Because if he had those,

298
00:14:18,350 --> 00:14:21,690
then he wouldn't have gotten himself in a situation involving black magic.

299
00:14:22,230 --> 00:14:23,870
What about you, Chilchuk?

300
00:14:24,010 --> 00:14:25,870
Why don't you try studying some magic?

301
00:14:26,230 --> 00:14:27,870
Maybe you'd stop being scared of it.

302
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:29,490
Oh, I am so sorry.

303
00:14:29,730 --> 00:14:32,410
You see, any half-foot I know who's dipped into black magic

304
00:14:32,410 --> 00:14:35,210
mysteriously got kidnapped by elves and were never seen again.

305
00:14:35,350 --> 00:14:36,690
It's such a crazy coincidence.

306
00:14:37,110 --> 00:14:39,350
Because of that, I've never had the chance to learn about it.

307
00:14:39,490 --> 00:14:41,090
Forgive me for being so ignorant.

308
00:14:41,210 --> 00:14:44,750
Actually, the ancient magic I've been researching isn't what you think.

309
00:14:45,110 --> 00:14:49,010
It's magic that draws energy from a different plane where infinity exists.

310
00:14:49,590 --> 00:14:52,190
How do you turn a cup that's full of water into gas?

311
00:14:52,410 --> 00:14:54,070
You simply boil it, right?

312
00:14:54,070 --> 00:14:58,290
Well, then how do you turn all the water in a lake into gas?

313
00:14:59,110 --> 00:15:02,610
The logic behind it's the same, but it's easier said than done.

314
00:15:03,790 --> 00:15:07,090
You need magic that supports vast amounts of power and time,

315
00:15:07,450 --> 00:15:09,130
which is what coordinate magic is.

316
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:12,630
Many places in this dungeon are linked to another place.

317
00:15:13,090 --> 00:15:15,030
That power is used to summon monsters,

318
00:15:15,670 --> 00:15:17,610
also to create the dungeon itself.

319
00:15:18,590 --> 00:15:22,250
At that time, Valon didn't have the power to recover on her own.

320
00:15:22,250 --> 00:15:25,190
In an attempt to circumvent that,

321
00:15:25,530 --> 00:15:27,810
I ended up rewriting a section of the dungeon

322
00:15:27,810 --> 00:15:30,170
and made it so that her body was part of it.

323
00:15:30,730 --> 00:15:32,210
Just for a moment, of course.

324
00:15:35,070 --> 00:15:36,170
Another earthquake.

325
00:15:36,630 --> 00:15:37,370
It's close.

326
00:15:38,550 --> 00:15:39,630
Look over there!

327
00:15:40,250 --> 00:15:41,230
The wall's moving.

328
00:15:42,530 --> 00:15:43,610
But where's it going?

329
00:15:44,370 --> 00:15:45,650
Let's get a closer look.

330
00:15:45,650 --> 00:15:51,630
Hey, what's wrong?

331
00:15:52,110 --> 00:15:53,610
I suddenly feel dizzy.

332
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:54,930
Oh, yeah, that's right!

333
00:15:55,310 --> 00:15:56,950
It was your first time using magic,

334
00:15:57,170 --> 00:15:59,210
so you're likely dealing with mana sickness.

335
00:15:59,670 --> 00:16:01,390
It'll hopefully ease up soon.

336
00:16:02,070 --> 00:16:02,990
We'll be back.

337
00:16:03,270 --> 00:16:04,090
Get rest, okay?

338
00:16:05,210 --> 00:16:07,170
Whether I open or close my eyes,

339
00:16:07,290 --> 00:16:08,990
everything looks so saturated.

340
00:16:08,990 --> 00:16:16,870
Am I seeing things?

341
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:18,410
Hearing things?

342
00:16:18,590 --> 00:16:21,330
I'm begging you just for a stay.

343
00:16:21,830 --> 00:16:24,990
Mana sickness really bites?

344
00:16:27,990 --> 00:16:30,110
The path in front of us is changing.

345
00:16:30,110 --> 00:16:32,670
I think I see a pattern.

346
00:16:33,250 --> 00:16:34,750
But then again, maybe not.

347
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:38,350
It's looking like we gotta observe things some more.

348
00:16:38,750 --> 00:16:42,110
Not being able to make progress is bad, but...

349
00:16:42,110 --> 00:16:42,230
Hmm?

350
00:16:43,910 --> 00:16:45,610
The floor's rising all of a sudden!

351
00:16:45,890 --> 00:16:46,970
Hurry and get off!

352
00:16:47,510 --> 00:16:48,070
Ow!

353
00:16:48,550 --> 00:16:50,010
That sure was close.

354
00:16:50,330 --> 00:16:52,330
And we almost got stuck there, huh?

355
00:16:52,330 --> 00:16:59,630
The cockatrice with merciless, petrifying venom.

356
00:17:04,390 --> 00:17:06,010
Sure looks like a basilisk!

357
00:17:06,090 --> 00:17:08,450
But it's a cockatrice, which is ten times more dangerous!

358
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:10,650
One bite from it, you'll turn into a statue!

359
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:13,010
Door to the left!

360
00:17:13,390 --> 00:17:14,510
Hurry and get inside!

361
00:17:14,510 --> 00:17:28,330
What are we gonna do?

362
00:17:28,850 --> 00:17:30,090
This won't hold long.

363
00:17:30,490 --> 00:17:32,290
Are we able to escape through the back?

364
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:35,210
If it has the same characteristics as a basilisk,

365
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:38,390
then I'm pretty sure it can detect us just by tracking our body heat.

366
00:17:39,450 --> 00:17:41,350
It'll be hard for us to sneak away.

367
00:17:41,350 --> 00:17:45,250
But that's only something the snakehead has the ability to do.

368
00:17:45,670 --> 00:17:47,910
The birdhead's relying on sight to find us.

369
00:17:48,690 --> 00:17:52,990
Marcil, do you remember what Laios did when we faced a basilisk the last time?

370
00:17:57,130 --> 00:17:59,370
Whatever you do, don't back down.

371
00:17:59,730 --> 00:18:02,290
Put your whole body and soul into intimidating it.

372
00:18:03,390 --> 00:18:05,310
That's easy for you to say.

373
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:07,830
All you gotta do is make yourself look big,

374
00:18:08,010 --> 00:18:09,770
and yell at it nice and strong!

375
00:18:09,770 --> 00:18:12,710
I get that I'm taller than Chilchuk and Senshi,

376
00:18:12,910 --> 00:18:16,290
but this monster's twice the size of a basilisk,

377
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:18,530
and I'm honestly not that good at yelling.

378
00:18:19,710 --> 00:18:22,130
Wait, what did Laios yell back then?

379
00:18:22,850 --> 00:18:23,650
Was it...

380
00:18:23,650 --> 00:18:25,670
Or...

381
00:18:25,670 --> 00:18:27,430
Maybe...

382
00:18:27,430 --> 00:18:32,610
Well, regardless of what it was,

383
00:18:32,830 --> 00:18:34,490
I've just gotta make it flinch!

384
00:18:34,490 --> 00:18:40,930
Roll credits.

385
00:18:41,470 --> 00:18:42,610
What am I even doing?

386
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,570
I'm definitely gonna screw it up!

387
00:18:44,910 --> 00:18:46,630
I can't do what Laios does!

388
00:18:46,710 --> 00:18:48,310
How am I supposed to do this?

389
00:18:49,910 --> 00:18:50,810
I know.

390
00:18:51,530 --> 00:18:52,770
I'll do it...

391
00:18:52,770 --> 00:18:54,850
My own way!

392
00:18:54,850 --> 00:19:00,950
The magic school's first-ever genius,

393
00:19:01,710 --> 00:19:02,070
Marcel!

394
00:19:05,310 --> 00:19:06,810
What was that explosion?

395
00:19:07,130 --> 00:19:07,610
It's Marcel!

396
00:19:08,050 --> 00:19:08,490
Come on!

397
00:19:08,490 --> 00:19:16,550
Too shallow!

398
00:19:16,550 --> 00:19:20,450
Crap, I made too much noise!

399
00:19:20,870 --> 00:19:22,550
Both heads are looking at me now!

400
00:19:23,030 --> 00:19:24,090
They need to cast,

401
00:19:24,210 --> 00:19:25,330
but there's no time...

402
00:19:25,330 --> 00:19:36,330
Marcel!

403
00:19:36,890 --> 00:19:37,970
Did you get bitten?

404
00:19:38,550 --> 00:19:39,610
I'm okay.

405
00:19:41,550 --> 00:19:43,770
That looks like a bite to me, you idiot!

406
00:19:44,470 --> 00:19:45,190
Damn it!

407
00:19:45,610 --> 00:19:46,070
What?

408
00:19:46,290 --> 00:19:48,010
You got bitten by a cockatrice?

409
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,170
This is bad.

410
00:19:49,510 --> 00:19:51,990
Do you know the trick to help you deal with a cockatrice bite?

411
00:19:52,690 --> 00:19:54,150
There's a trick to it?

412
00:19:54,150 --> 00:19:55,890
First, remove your pants.

413
00:19:57,210 --> 00:19:59,330
Sit and bring your body close together.

414
00:20:01,030 --> 00:20:02,390
Pull your arms inward.

415
00:20:02,870 --> 00:20:04,170
Cover your ears with your fingers.

416
00:20:04,610 --> 00:20:05,550
And close your mouth.

417
00:20:08,870 --> 00:20:09,470
Good.

418
00:20:09,790 --> 00:20:11,470
Now you're all set to turn into stone.

419
00:20:12,030 --> 00:20:15,150
I thought this was a method not to get petrified, you little...

420
00:20:16,370 --> 00:20:20,890
Oh, crap.

421
00:20:20,890 --> 00:20:23,290
She got hardened in a really dangerous pose.

422
00:20:23,290 --> 00:20:24,290
She's gonna break.

423
00:20:24,410 --> 00:20:27,210
Her core is unbalanced, so she could tip over any second.

424
00:20:27,710 --> 00:20:29,030
Not looking good.

425
00:20:29,850 --> 00:20:32,030
Of all the poses she could have chosen.

426
00:20:32,670 --> 00:20:33,910
What should we do now?

427
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:35,930
Is there any way to undo this?

428
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:38,370
There's a few ways.

429
00:20:38,870 --> 00:20:40,690
First is waiting till it just wears off.

430
00:20:41,830 --> 00:20:44,330
Petrification's more like a curse instead of a poison.

431
00:20:44,970 --> 00:20:46,830
Elves have a strong resistance to magic,

432
00:20:46,830 --> 00:20:49,130
so they should recover faster than others.

433
00:20:50,050 --> 00:20:52,750
The second way is to search for some medicinal herbs.

434
00:20:53,230 --> 00:20:56,370
Or third, to go look for an adventurer who knows the right spell.

435
00:20:57,130 --> 00:21:00,630
Last option is to let me try to cast something to heal her.

436
00:21:01,470 --> 00:21:02,290
Can you, though?

437
00:21:02,290 --> 00:21:05,390
Marcel taught me the basics of reading her magic book.

438
00:21:06,010 --> 00:21:07,970
There should be a spell to get her back to normal.

439
00:21:10,550 --> 00:21:13,050
Well, while looking for herbs and an adventurer,

440
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:15,450
I'll stay hopeful about the other two ideas.

441
00:21:16,050 --> 00:21:18,310
So, how long would it take to heal up naturally?

442
00:21:19,310 --> 00:21:21,550
For Tallman, it's six months to ten years.

443
00:21:21,550 --> 00:21:23,930
I'm gonna fetch the cockatrice.

444
00:21:26,930 --> 00:21:29,250
These changed color real fast overnight.

445
00:21:29,670 --> 00:21:31,350
We should eat them sooner than later.

446
00:21:32,170 --> 00:21:34,170
She's leaning, and it's kind of concerning.

447
00:21:34,870 --> 00:21:37,390
Should we put something underneath her butt to keep her up straight?

448
00:21:37,990 --> 00:21:39,090
Yeah, that might help.

449
00:21:39,330 --> 00:21:40,610
I've got a pretty good idea.

450
00:21:41,270 --> 00:21:42,630
At the bottom of the pan,

451
00:21:42,770 --> 00:21:45,030
place the julienned flower buds and some spices.

452
00:21:45,670 --> 00:21:47,550
And place Marcel on top of that.

453
00:21:48,770 --> 00:21:50,790
Oh, her eyelashes broke.

454
00:21:50,790 --> 00:21:52,610
Soak the cockatrice meat in a brine

455
00:21:52,610 --> 00:21:54,350
and place that in Marcel's lap.

456
00:21:54,710 --> 00:21:57,050
And this way, she stays perfectly balanced.

457
00:21:59,670 --> 00:22:01,750
Well, she does seem more stable.

458
00:22:02,470 --> 00:22:04,030
This should keep her from taking a tumble.

459
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:06,890
She looks kind of like a heretic idol.

460
00:22:07,570 --> 00:22:08,730
From that point on,

461
00:22:08,830 --> 00:22:10,550
Laios and the others worked hard.

462
00:22:11,550 --> 00:22:13,510
There were many trials and errors.

463
00:22:15,230 --> 00:22:17,110
But on the fourth day...

464
00:22:17,110 --> 00:22:17,910
They found one!

465
00:22:18,310 --> 00:22:20,090
How do you reckon you use it?

466
00:22:20,090 --> 00:22:24,690
Uh, how about we stick him on?

467
00:22:25,650 --> 00:22:27,570
The stone is starting to feel a little warm.

468
00:22:28,390 --> 00:22:29,230
Now's the time.

469
00:22:30,910 --> 00:22:38,430
Am I even pronouncing any of this correctly?

470
00:22:38,430 --> 00:22:39,070
Crap!

471
00:22:48,750 --> 00:22:49,850
Marcel, you're back!

472
00:22:49,910 --> 00:22:50,830
Yep, soft.

473
00:22:51,130 --> 00:22:52,330
I said the word's right!

474
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:53,590
Wait, huh?

475
00:22:53,930 --> 00:22:54,910
What the...

476
00:22:54,910 --> 00:22:56,350
Is this a vegetable?

477
00:22:56,810 --> 00:22:58,010
Why is there a pot?

478
00:22:58,590 --> 00:22:59,790
Let's see here.

479
00:23:00,310 --> 00:23:00,570
Hmm.

480
00:23:01,110 --> 00:23:02,830
This one was a success, too!

481
00:23:03,050 --> 00:23:03,330
Yay!

482
00:23:03,330 --> 00:23:07,790
Boil the meat that you had brine in, and then slice it up thinly.

483
00:23:08,510 --> 00:23:12,810
Take the fermented buds, plate them with the meat, and it's ready.

484
00:23:12,810 --> 00:23:15,730
What?

485
00:23:16,270 --> 00:23:17,530
It's really been that long?

486
00:23:17,970 --> 00:23:20,370
I wonder what method ended up working in the end.

487
00:23:20,650 --> 00:23:22,710
No way to tell when we tried so many.

488
00:23:23,130 --> 00:23:25,330
It'd be nice if it was the spell I cast.

489
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:26,450
Yeah, right.

490
00:23:26,590 --> 00:23:28,670
It was probably all thanks to the herb I found.

491
00:23:28,670 --> 00:23:29,410
You sure?

492
00:23:29,910 --> 00:23:33,530
Because maybe their cockatries mean I was prepping somehow neutralize the curse.

493
00:23:33,530 --> 00:23:38,850
I caused them so much trouble, and at a time when we really needed to get back to the surface.

494
00:23:39,610 --> 00:23:40,750
Hey, guys, I...

495
00:23:40,750 --> 00:23:42,730
No, wait a second.

496
00:23:43,490 --> 00:23:46,770
Under the circumstances, there's something I should tell them first.

497
00:23:47,570 --> 00:23:48,670
Yeah, of course.

498
00:23:50,230 --> 00:23:52,890
Don't ever use people as a human pickling weight.

499
00:23:53,970 --> 00:23:58,410
So it goes with dungeon food delicious in dungeon.

